

                               WHAT IS TABS?

TABS  is  a  900 service that will allow your callers to get instant access
upgrades  by simply calling a 900 number.  The will be given an access code
to  enter in this door and it will automatically upgrade their access.  The
caller  will be charged $10.00 on their phonebill, and as such they need to
be 18 or older, or have their parent's permission to use this utility.






                            HOW DO I SET IT UP?

Create  a  directory  in  Doors:   called TABS and place the executable and
config  file inside.  You can edit this config file to indicate what access
groups should be given when a caller validates their access code.

The  config  file consists of 32 lines.  The first is the seven digit phone
number  for your BBS that they will use when they call the 900 number.  The
remaining  31  lines  are  for  access  groups  1  through 31.  Group 32 is
excluded,  since  you can't go anywhere from sysop access anyway :-) If you
don't  want  a particular access group to be upgraded, then set the upgrade
level equal to the current user level.

For example:

929-8154
1 2
2 3
3 4
4 5
5 5
6 6
7 7
8 8
9 9
...
29 29
30 30
31 31

The  first  line is my BBS phone number.  Lines 2 through 5 tell Excel_TABS
to upgrade levels 1 through 4 to the next higher access level.  The rest of
the  lines  tell  Excel_TABS  not to allow upgrading of those access levels
through the TABS system.





                       HOW DO I GET MY ACCESS CODES?

Unarchive the included TABSINFO.LHA and read the enclosed agreements.  Mail
or fax your signed form and you will be on your way to having automated 900
access service on your BBS.



